    `Father, I bring to You today the things that feel wasted — the years, the efforts, the prayers, the relationships, the opportunities that seemed to close before they opened, the suffering that has not yet produced a visible good. I bring them to Romans 8:28 honestly — not as a quick comfort but as a genuine, sustained trust that You are working in all of them, for my good, according to a purpose that exceeds what I can currently see. Let me have the faith of Joseph — who held the dream through thirteen years of evidence against it and arrived at the throne room with the character that only the pit and the prison could have produced. And let me receive the gift that Job received — not necessarily an explanation, but a seeing. The encounter with who You are that makes the explanation unnecessary. Nothing is wasted in Your hands. Not one day. Not one tear. I trust You with all of it.`
